{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;proposal\r\nby reason of subdivision of front garden space would interrupt the pattern and\r\ngrain of development within the Christchurch Avenue&amp;nbsp; street scene, contrary to the high quality\r\ndesign aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies\r\nD3.D (1) and D3.D (11) of the London Plan (2021), Policy CS1.B of the Harrow\r\nCore Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Polices\r\nLocal Plan (2013) and the Residential Design Guide Supplementary Planning\r\nDocument (2010).&lt;/span&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The proposed development would be inappropriately\r\nconfigured, with the kitchen, living, dining area of the loft level flats being\r\nsited directly above the bedroom 2 of the first floor flat below and proposed\r\nbedroom 2 at first floor now next door to the living room of the first floor\r\nflat, giving rise to impacts of harmful noise transference. The proposed\r\ndevelopment would therefore be contrary to the high quality design aspirations\r\nof the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 D .7 of the\r\nLondon Plan, Policies DM1 C, DM1 D (g), DM26 A (b) and DM26 E of the Harrow\r\nDevelopment Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of an Insufficient Flood Risk Assessment, fails demonstrate that the proposed development would effectively manage and mitigate flood risk on site or on the adjacent properties, and that it would not create an unacceptable level of flood risk.&amp;nbsp; The proposed development would therefore be contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), policy SI 12 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1 U of Harrow Core Strategy (2012) policies DM 9 and DM10 of the Harrow Development Management Polices Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development by virtue of proposed entrance to the additional flat located to the rear of the building would present an impractical and unsafe access point. The proposed development would therefore be contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 D .7 of the London Plan, Policies DM1 C, DM1 D (g), DM26 A (b) and DM26 E of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
